/*
 * Batman_Panel — self-contained Cloudflare Worker (ES module).
 * Paste this ENTIRE file into the Cloudflare Workers code editor and deploy.
 * REQUIRED dashboard bindings: D1 database as DB, KV namespace as CACHE.
 * RECOMMENDED: add a Cron trigger every five minutes to repair stale
 * connection counters and remove expired sessions automatically.
 * FIRST VISITOR picks the administrator username and password on first launch.
 * SECURITY: With no setup token, an unclaimed Worker can be taken over by
 * whoever reaches its URL first. Complete setup immediately after deployment.
 * If upgrading an old installation, temporarily retain its original
 * BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN Secret and log in once (username defaults to admin) to upgrade.
 * No ASSETS binding, npm install, SQL console migration or extra file is needed.
 * Designed for Cloudflare Free limits, not unlimited/free at any traffic:
 * check your current Worker/D1/KV usage in the account dashboard.
 * IP Test > Auto-Resolve performs DNS-only lookup of real Cloudflare
 * candidate IPs (NOT proxy validation). The previous browser-image scanner
 * was removed. For actual private-route checks, create a dedicated agent
 * token and run the embedded /tools/personal-agent.mjs on the TARGET network
 * with Node.js 20+. The optional 40/80-IP target-network scout first
 * checks public TLS/SNI + WebSocket twice, then separately queues a 4/4
 * VLESS+Trojan job for up to ten unverified finalists. Leave the agent
 * running for both stages; public-edge RTT is NOT proxy latency/health.
 * v1.8 adds live authenticated job progress (which does NOT qualify IPs),
 * edge failure stages, balanced/latency/stability shortlist modes,
 * an admin-only on-demand per-IP evidence table + credential-free CSV,
 * and per-protocol RTT evidence. Client-side measurements are not guaranteed.
 * Optional Xray WebSocket Early Data via ?ed=1024 is available ONLY via
 * the explicitly selected ED subscription / JSON: default links unchanged.
 * Unsupported: raw UDP, QUIC, REALITY, XHTTP and HTTPUpgrade transports.
 * Optional 128/256/512 KiB two-way traffic samples pass
 * through BOTH VLESS and Trojan; they consume user quota, need explicit
 * selection, and are short measurements, never a guaranteed future speed.
 * Only an opted-in private pool and opt-in optimizer can automatically
 * replace subscription IPs after qualifying real VLESS+Trojan reports.
 * Static imported URIs require client subscription refresh to update.
 * Shared-pool checking stays separate: Status > /tools/probe.mjs.
 * IP configs are enabled by default but only use timely checked/reported IPs.
 * Raw Trojan TCP/UDP are not supported; VLESS and Trojan use WS/TLS for TCP.
 * This script includes the original bat emblem, three Gotham city backdrops,
 * Vazirmatn fonts, a QR generator and license texts served at /licenses/*.
 */
